# Curated "grammar word" lists for the Sample Lists tab — closed classes
# (pronouns, conjunctions, prepositions, ...) whose membership is small and
# fixed. Unlike the other sample lists these are NOT translations: each target
# language has its own table, written by hand, and a list is just the words of
# one category in one language. Nothing here is generated by Gemini, so adding
# one of these lists is instant and free.
#
# Each row is (word, label). The label is a short grammatical description in
# English, stored as the pair's "source word". It tells the learner (and the
# question writer) which role this form plays — e.g. `las` is a feminine plural
# direct object pronoun — and is never put into a quiz sentence.
#
# Authoring rules:
# - one row per word form per category, so the quiz's duplicate-target
#   collapsing never removes anything;
# - no apostrophes in a word (typed apostrophes vary by keyboard);
# - a word that plays two roles (Spanish `la`: article and pronoun) belongs to
#   each category it serves, as a separate row in that category's list.

